[2026-03-04T20:25:39.516Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019FpBokVoWzeNNd3jxZmZAo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Skill\n     2→\n     3→You are implementing a package script based on its design doc in `skills/scripts/`.\n     4→\n     5→## Process\n     6→\n     7→1. **Read the design doc**: Read `skills/scripts/<script-name>.md` to understand the\n     8→   script's purpose, usage, behavior, inputs, outputs, and implementation tips.\n     9→\n    10→2. **Read related code**: Before writing, read existing scripts and modules referenced in\n    11→   the design doc's implementation tips. Understand the patterns already in use.\n    12→\n    13→3. **Implement the script**: Write the script as a TypeScript file at `scripts/<script-name>.ts`.\n    14→   Scripts MUST be TypeScript run via `tsx`. Do not write shell scripts.\n    15→\n    16→4. **Add the package.json entry**: Add the script to the app's `package.json` under `\"scripts\"`,\n    17→   matching the usage section of the design doc.\n    18→\n    19→5. **Test the script**: Run the script to verify it works. If it modifies state (database,\n    20→   files, processes), verify the state changes are correct.\n    21→\n    22→6. **Typecheck and lint**: Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx eslint .` to verify no errors.\n    23→\n    24→7. Verify the script works end-to-end.\n    25→\n    26→## Guidelines\n    27→\n    28→- Follow the design doc's contract exactly. The design doc defines the expected inputs, outputs,\n    29→  and behavior — do not deviate from it without updating the design doc.\n    30→- Reuse existing infrastructure. If the design doc says to use `initSchema` or other shared\n    31→  modules, import them rather than duplicating logic.\n    32→- Handle errors clearly. Scripts should fail with descriptive error messages when required\n    33→  environment variables are missing or external calls fail.\n    34→- Scripts must work from the app directory (`apps/<AppName>/`). Use relative paths for local\n    35→  files and respect the monorepo structure.\n    36→- Scripts MUST be TypeScript. Use Node.js APIs (`child_process`, `fs`, `path`, etc.) for\n    37→  any process management, file I/O, or CLI invocations. Do not write shell scripts.\n    38→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"716202eb-4d7a-44be-b0c3-e090898a2525","uuid":"624ea176-61aa-4d7f-87f0-62c0048314aa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/tasks/writeScript.md","content":"# Skill\n\nYou are implementing a package script based on its design doc in `skills/scripts/`.\n\n## Process\n\n1. **Read the design doc**: Read `skills/scripts/<script-name>.md` to understand the\n   script's purpose, usage, behavior, inputs, outputs, and implementation tips.\n\n2. **Read related code**: Before writing, read existing scripts and modules referenced in\n   the design doc's implementation tips. Understand the patterns already in use.\n\n3. **Implement the script**: Write the script as a TypeScript file at `scripts/<script-name>.ts`.\n   Scripts MUST be TypeScript run via `tsx`. Do not write shell scripts.\n\n4. **Add the package.json entry**: Add the script to the app's `package.json` under `\"scripts\"`,\n   matching the usage section of the design doc.\n\n5. **Test the script**: Run the script to verify it works. If it modifies state (database,\n   files, processes), verify the state changes are correct.\n\n6. **Typecheck and lint**: Run `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx eslint .` to verify no errors.\n\n7. Verify the script works end-to-end.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- Follow the design doc's contract exactly. The design doc defines the expected inputs, outputs,\n  and behavior — do not deviate from it without updating the design doc.\n- Reuse existing infrastructure. If the design doc says to use `initSchema` or other shared\n  modules, import them rather than duplicating logic.\n- Handle errors clearly. Scripts should fail with descriptive error messages when required\n  environment variables are missing or external calls fail.\n- Scripts must work from the app directory (`apps/<AppName>/`). Use relative paths for local\n  files and respect the monorepo structure.\n- Scripts MUST be TypeScript. Use Node.js APIs (`child_process`, `fs`, `path`, etc.) for\n  any process management, file I/O, or CLI invocations. Do not write shell scripts.\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
